      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not define “social age” as a general “place in the socially patterned stages of life.” It only mentions that participants’ reported goals/concerns “reflect different social age systems or developmental tasks,” without providing a definition of the term’s meaning.",
        "The definition’s general framing about “different developmental or role-related priorities” and “education and work in younger adulthood versus broader social concerns in older adulthood” is only partially supported by the specific results reported (e.g., younger adults’ tasks tied to education/profession; older adults’ tasks tied to world issues/war/terrorism). The packet does not support the broader, general life-stage characterization in the first sentence."
